I go from the meat counter to the shelves.
I still need three things for the potato salad.
First, I fetch the potatoes.
I take a bag of waxy potatoes.
Then I look for the mustard.
I find a small jar on the bottom shelf.
Afterwards, I only need mayonnaise.
A jar stands right next to it, and I pack it.
I go to the till and put my things on the belt.
"Hello," the cashier says to me.
"Hello," I reply.
She pulls my groceries over the scanner.
"That is thirteen Euro and forty cents, please," she says.
I pay with my card.
"Do you need the receipt?" she asks me.
"Yes, please," I say.
She gives it to me.
I open the backpack.
Carefully, I pack my groceries into the backpack.
I put the meat right at the top.
